id: pmc-tracker-milestones
title: Generate release notes from immutable tracker milestones
description: Add a backend-neutral immutable release source and a tracker milestone creation command for plain-directory and SDK database snapshots.
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: added,changelog,no-git
created_at: "2026-10-21T18:17:49.989Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T19:25:50.685Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Plain-directory and synthetic database milestones generate identical notes; changed milestone membership refuses; git-tag behavior remains separately tested; typed SDK and CLI create and generate without git; compact agent receipts and typed refusals with remedies; README and example; measured validation on a read-only public tracker copy; npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds; behavioral revert proof.
comments[28]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T18:18:35.166Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against the pinned core SDK and sibling pm-context and pm-web packages: workspace snapshots store and verify tracker state; context receipts store bounded context reads; changelog --group-by milestone uses mutable item metadata and tracker-only input lacks a first-class immutable release source. None supplies frozen release membership and late-close attribution. Implement an atomic immutable store contract, a directory adapter, SDK snapshot input and a real SQLite test adapter; preserve existing git-tag tests and add no-git regressions."
  "2026-10-21T18:24:44.292Z",codex-agent,"Focused tests passed 4/4, including real SQLite versus directory parity, concurrent no-replace publication, changed membership refusal, fingerprint verification and real initialized tracker creation/generation with PATH containing no git executable. Public origin/main tracker validation at 56f8536702f6d3266825534d502a3dfc947cfb83: 189 scanned and frozen members, 165 emitted entries, 4 excluded non-change closures, 1 populated release section, 13229 markdown bytes, 34582 summary JSON bytes; repeat output byte-identical; changed membership refused; all 387 source files unchanged on a read-only copy. Full coverage and required release gates are pending."
  "2026-10-21T18:27:06.107Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof on isolated source copies: removing only the createReleaseMilestone changed-membership refusal makes the real directory/SQLite regression fail with Missing expected rejection (exit 1); reverting only resolveTrackerReleaseHistory frozen-row selection to current rows makes the same regression fail on emitted entry count (exit 1). Production source stayed intact. Actual pinned pm host milestone create passed in both JSON and TOON modes with no git on PATH; standalone generate and summary also passed."
  "2026-10-21T18:30:01.759Z",codex-agent,The no-git acceptance check also exposed pre-existing explicit tag requests silently falling back outside a repository. Added a preflight refusal in assertReleaseTagHistory naming the git requirement and the tracker-only and milestone alternatives; retained full tag-specific regression coverage. Added a duplicate-name refusal to the pure milestone resolver to prevent repeated boundary input from duplicating rendered notes.
  "2026-10-21T18:33:47.250Z",codex-agent,"Final focused feature run passed 4/4 with the milestone module at 100% lines, branches and functions. The tracked pm test execution also passed 4/4 with reported_tests evidence. All 180 declarations passed the docstring gate. A third isolated behavioral revert removed only the missing-git preflight from assertReleaseTagHistory and failed the no-git regression with Missing expected exception (exit 1). Process tracing confirmed milestone host create and standalone generation did not execute git; the only git probe in fixture setup was the upstream SDK initializer."
  "2026-10-21T18:35:57.552Z",codex-agent,"Overlap was additionally verified against the installed current core CLI/SDK 2026.10.21: its public workspace-snapshot surface provides create/inspect/list/restore/delete storage and still has no changelog release attribution source. The implementation retains the repository-pinned 2026.10.19 dependency as required. The full coverage run has reproduced the existing pmc-redos-startup-231 worker readiness failures; parser and coverage thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T18:46:31.571Z",codex-agent,"Draft PR 265 opened at ec3580e70c3140550fc9191d4f1a9d91e85fd50b. CI on Node 22 and 26 passed all package checks; each coverage suite passed 786/786 with zero failures or skips and 100% lines, branches and functions across all 15 measured source files. Tracker health, docstrings, production audit, package contents, changelog links/date and publish attestation passed. Local npm, Bun and clean-HOME release commands are running sequentially; their final receipts remain pending. No merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-21T18:58:13.284Z",codex-agent,"Added a production history edge case: an ID selected while open closes in a later immutable snapshot, then reopens in the current tracker. The new real directory/SQLite regression failed before the fix (2 emitted entries instead of 3). The resolver now retains the first captured closed row across all milestones while preserving ownership by the first containing milestone. Stopped the in-progress local gate queue so it cannot be mistaken for final-source evidence; the required gates will restart after this source change is verified."
  "2026-10-21T19:00:32.334Z",codex-agent,"The captured-late-close/reopen regression now passes on both real directory and SQLite stores. Focused suite: 4/4, zero skips, milestone module 100% lines/branches/functions. Reverting only the captured-completion lookup to first-snapshot/current-row selection fails the regression with 2 entries instead of 3. The original membership-refusal and frozen-evidence reverts still fail independently. This is a fourth behavioral revert proof including the unchanged missing-git guard proof."
  "2026-10-21T19:22:58.575Z",codex-agent,"Final-source npm run release:check completed on Node 26.12.0/npm 11.20.0: 775/786 tests passed, 11 worker-readiness failures, zero skips; all 15 measured source files reached 100% lines, branches and functions. Exit 1 is retained. The same source commit 327e91e passed all 786/786 tests and all workflow gates on both Node 22 and Node 26 CI runners. Bun and clean-HOME commands are pending; no thresholds or parser budgets were changed."
  "2026-10-21T19:31:09.759Z",codex-agent,"Additional real Bun 1.3.5 runtime acceptance passed on final source: both the compiled standalone CLI and the typed SDK loaded and generated one expected entry from an SDK-initialized plain-directory tracker, with PATH containing no git executable. This verifies Bun execution directly in addition to bun run release:check, whose full-suite receipt is still pending. The repeated read-only public validation retained 189 frozen members, 165 notes, four excluded non-change closures and byte-identical output; all 387 source files stayed unchanged."
  "2026-10-21T19:40:16.019Z",codex-agent,"Final-source bun run release:check completed: 783/786 tests passed, three worker-readiness failures, zero skips; all 15 measured source files reached 100% lines, branches and functions. Exit 1 is retained. Direct Bun 1.3.5 CLI and SDK runtime smoke checks both passed on a real no-git tracker. The clean-HOME npm release command is running. Raw SDK snapshots omit physical folder enrichment; custom-type TOON references remain a separate integration follow-up under pmc-rspo (neutral references work by default; SDK callers can supply itemTypeFolders)."
  "2026-10-21T19:46:40.140Z",codex-agent,"Final local release receipts at unchanged thresholds on Node 26.12.0: npm run release:check exited 1 with 775/786 passing and 11 worker-startup failures; bun run release:check exited 1 with 783/786 passing and three worker-startup failures; clean-HOME npm run release:check with global/system git configuration disabled exited 1 with 783/786 passing and three worker-startup failures. Every run had zero skips and 100% lines, branches and functions across all 15 measured source files. All failures occur at the existing 5000ms worker-readiness deadline (pmc-redos-startup-231); no parser CPU-budget or feature assertion failed. The same source commit 327e91e passed 786/786 and every workflow gate on Node 22 and 26 CI. Direct Bun CLI/SDK and four behavioral reverts are verified. Statement coverage remains unmeasured by the existing gate; custom-folder TOON registry enrichment stays under pmc-rspo. PR 265 remains draft, with no merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T20:25:49.578Z",codex-agent,"PR 265 review round: remote branch pulled first; main is already an ancestor. Read all comments in all three unresolved threads and the latest CodeRabbit review body (no outside-diff or nitpick sections). Valid findings: normalized conflict option keys, ICU-dependent fingerprint ordering, and missing file flush before hard-link publication. Plan: regressions and independent behavioral revert proofs, inspect the complete PR for matching defects, rebuild dist, targeted local verification only, then CI npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds. No thread replies/resolutions, merge or release."
  "2026-10-21T20:27:53.856Z",codex-agent,"Review fixes implemented: conflict guard checks kebab and camel keys; canonical object keys, selected IDs and same-time boundary names use UTF-16 code-unit comparison; directory publication exclusively opens, writes, syncs and closes before linking, then syncs/closes the directory. Temp cleanup covers write and sync errors; tests use real filesystem operations with injected failures, real SQLite, and an actual no-git host CLI. Focused tests pass 6/6, typecheck/build:test pass, docstrings pass 18 files/180 declarations; git diff --check passes. No lint script or linter config is present. CI now invokes unchanged npm run release:check and bun run release:check on both Node versions; full gates stay off the saturated local host."
  "2026-10-21T20:29:32.512Z",codex-agent,"Independent behavioral revert proofs against the review-round source: (1) restoring only the old milestone conflict guard makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"real plain tracker\" test/milestones.test.ts fail (exit 1): camel allReleaseTags reaches the missing-git path instead of milestone_options. (2) Reverting only canonical makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"milestone fingerprints\" test/milestones.test.ts fail (exit 1): actual digest 68a006d1 differs from fixed fixture 44c1178e. (3) Reverting only selectItems makes that test fail: A,ä,z instead of A,z,ä. (4) Reverting only resolveTrackerReleaseHistory makes that test fail: a owns the tied release instead of Z. (5) Reverting only DirectoryReleaseMilestoneStore.publish makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"directory publication syncs\" test/milestones.test.ts fail (exit 1): only link is observed instead of write, file sync/close, link, directory sync/close. All five changed regions were reverted separately with other fixes retained; source was restored in finally blocks. These assertions execute TypeScript source; compiled dist was rebuilt for the actual host CLI acceptance. pm test pmc-tracker-milestones --run --match \"node --test test/milestones.test.ts\" --progress also passed 6/6 with no skips (reported_tests receipt; automatic durable test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment retains the result)."
  "2026-10-21T20:36:21.944Z",codex-agent,"Review-round CI receipt at source head 5c46be47c9619772b418e7a84875ae3f15175bed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/39670999823 completed successfully. Both Node 22 and Node 26 jobs passed npm run release:check AND bun run release:check, each 788/788 tests, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across all 15 measured source files. Four complete gate executions total 3152 passing tests. Tracker health, docstrings (18 files/180 declarations), production audit, pack, generated changelog/link/date checks and publish attestation passed. CodeQL passed separately. Latest targeted coverage run also passed 6/6 with milestone module 100% lines/branches/functions; no local timeouts occurred this round. Local health additionally sees an installed pm-github host-version skew; clean CI health passed without that environment-only warning. All three findings and two self-review instances are fixed, with five independent failing reverts recorded above. No additional outside-diff or nitpick findings existed in the latest CodeRabbit body. Fresh CodeRabbit review was skipped and Greptile trial expired; those are not approvals. Existing statement-coverage and custom-folder limits remain under pmc-ilrh and pmc-rspo. No PM CLI/SDK bug was found during this round. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains in_progress. This final evidence-only commit will receive its own CI run before reporting the final head."
  "2026-10-21T22:47:28.128Z",codex-agent,"PR 265 review round: verified both unresolved threads PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6u-qSE and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6u-qSZ against the current branch. Normalize JSON snapshot data before fingerprinting; skip unsupported Windows directory sync while retaining temporary-file fsync and POSIX directory durability. Latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff or nitpick section. Audit the complete PR diff for these defect classes; add behavioral regressions and isolated revert proofs. Run targeted tests, typechecks and docstring lint locally; use unchanged npm and Bun CI release gates for full-suite evidence. No thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-21T22:51:36.098Z",codex-agent,"Both valid current review findings fixed. createReleaseMilestone hashes a JSON-normalized item snapshot. Self-review found the same raw-object mismatch in parseReleaseMilestone: normalize before validation and fingerprint verification, returning that verified representation. Rich adapter reads and persisted JSON now agree for Date, custom toJSON, undefined/sparse array entries and NaN/Infinity. Parser rejects cyclic and BigInt data with milestone_invalid. Windows publication preserves file write/fsync/close and hard-link ordering while skipping only directory open/fsync; POSIX sync and cleanup checks remain. Updated the SDK storage contract. Targeted tests passed 8/8, zero skips; npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run docstring (18 files, 180 declarations) and git diff --check passed. No lint script/config exists; no local timeout occurred. Full PR diff reviewed for JSON identity and publication durability defects; no further instances found."
  "2026-10-21T22:51:42.936Z",codex-agent,"Three independent behavioral revert proofs, restoring only one original function at a time while retaining the other fixes: (1) createReleaseMilestone revert: node --test --test-name-pattern \"milestone JSON snapshots\" test/milestones.test.ts exits 1 with milestone_invalid fingerprint mismatch during rich snapshot creation. (2) parseReleaseMilestone revert: the same command exits 1 with fingerprint mismatch on the rich remote-adapter read. (3) DirectoryReleaseMilestoneStore.publish revert: node --test --test-name-pattern \"Windows directory publication\" test/milestones.test.ts exits 1 with milestone_storage after attempted directory access. Each run had exactly one failing test and no skips. Fixed source restored in a finally block after every variant; tests execute TypeScript source, and committed dist was rebuilt for actual host CLI acceptance."
  "2026-10-21T22:53:15.679Z",codex-agent,"Final restored-source verification: pm test pmc-tracker-milestones --run --match \"node --test test/milestones.test.ts\" --progress passed 8/8 with zero failures/skips (reported_tests receipt). Durable test-result tracking is disabled, so this comment retains the result. Removed the obsolete undefined-key filter from canonical serialization because JSON normalization already removes undefined object fields. Rebuilt dist and reran build:test, typecheck, docstring lint (18 files/180 declarations) and whitespace checks successfully. Local health has the existing pm-github host-version skew plus the exact legacy provenance baseline; no merge receipts or history drift. Clean CI health and four unchanged full release gates (npm/Bun on Node 22/26) remain required after push. No new PM CLI/SDK bug found."
  "2026-10-21T23:01:46.818Z",codex-agent,"Review-round source head 53af886f065e71fba3dd0cec1b2a7510f6c3f995 passed CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/39689851925. Node 22 and Node 26 each passed npm run release:check and bun run release:check, 790/790 tests per gate, zero failures/skips; four complete gates total 3160 passing test executions. Every gate measured 100% lines, branches and functions across all 15 measured source files. Tracker health, docstrings (18 files/180 declarations), production audit, package contents, changelog links/date and publish attestation passed. Both unresolved findings and the additional parser instance are fixed; three independent behavioral reverts failed and restored-source pm-linked tests passed 8/8. No outside-diff or nitpick finding was present in the latest review body read for this round. No local timeout occurred. Existing statement coverage (pmc-ilrh) and custom-folder enrichment (pmc-rspo) limits remain; Windows behavior was tested by platform fault injection using real filesystem operations. No new PM CLI/SDK defect found. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification without closing the in_progress item. This receipt-only commit will receive its own full CI verification before the final report. No thread replies/resolutions, merge or release."
  "2026-10-22T09:33:43.970Z",codex-agent,"PR 265 review round: pulled remote head; main is already an ancestor. Fetched all four unresolved threads with every comment and latest CodeRabbit review; no outside-diff section. Confirmed count projections use live rows instead of resolved milestone rows, CI lacks direct Bun CLI/SDK execution, and README incorrectly promises unchanged tag behavior. Fix all instances; verify frozen deleted/reopened closures, explicit tag documentation and workflow invocation with independent failing reverts. Full npm and Bun release gates retain existing thresholds."
  "2026-10-22T09:35:53.983Z",codex-agent,"Review regressions passed 28/28 and direct Bun CLI/SDK smoke passed 2/2 on a real plain tracker. Four independent reverts: restoring only CLI main count expressions fails milestone JSON counts (0 instead of 2); restoring only extension run count expressions independently fails (0 instead of 2); restoring README tag-behavior paragraph fails milestone documentation; restoring CI Bun steps fails CI retains test. Each node --test --test-name-pattern command exits 1 with one failure, fixed files restored in finally. Full PR self-review found the same raw-row count in both semver explanation branches and extension summary/semver; every call site now uses generationOptions.items, covering Git-resolved rows too. No other matching defect found. Latest review contains no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-10-22T09:46:39.239Z",codex-agent,"The clean-HOME npm release gate is running at unchanged thresholds and has reproduced the existing 5000ms ReDoS worker-startup timeouts under host load. Retain this failure receipt; require passing npm and Bun full CI gates before the next PR. Exact independent revert commands: node --test --test-name-pattern \"milestone JSON counts\" test/milestones.test.ts (CLI main and extension run restored separately); node --test --test-name-pattern \"milestone documentation\" test/milestones.test.ts (README paragraph); node --test --test-name-pattern \"CI retains\" test/release-workflow.test.ts (CI steps). All four reverts exited 1; restored-source pm-linked suite passed 28/28. Local health retains only the existing pm-github host-version skew and exact 32-event legacy provenance baseline."
  "2026-10-22T09:51:40.013Z",codex-agent,"Source head 52044626cb558cb32088431ae874bdbac79f8531 passed CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/39758047933: npm run release:check and bun run release:check on Node 22 and 26 each passed 793/793 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, 100% lines/branches/functions across 15 measured source files. Four full gates total 3172 passing test executions. Direct Bun CLI and SDK smoke passed 2/2 on each job. Tracker health, docstrings (18 files/180 declarations), audit, pack, changelog/link/date and attestation checks passed. Local clean-HOME npm attempt reproduced existing 5000ms ReDoS worker startup timeouts and was stopped after all four CI gates passed; it is not a passing local gate receipt. Four independent failing reverts and restored 28/28 focused tests recorded above. All four unresolved findings fixed; no new threads appeared on recheck. Existing statement coverage and folder enrichment limitations remain under pmc-ilrh and pmc-rspo. No new SDK bug found; pm files multi-path invocation rejected extra arguments, corrected with structured single-file links. Release claim for orchestrator verification without closing item."
  "2026-10-22T19:20:59.097Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up review after orchestrator extension: rechecked clean worktree and released in-progress item, pulled remote 40a63c87 and merged origin/main because the branch was behind by one dependency/template commit. npm ci passed with zero audit vulnerabilities; pins were not independently changed. Previously fixed findings remain complete. New unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6vLTfT is valid: non-git recoveryCommands contains a shell placeholder and alternative workflows rather than executable tag-history repairs. Return an empty list, retain alternatives in the message, clarify usage/release recovery docs. New real plain-tracker regression covers all three tag flags with git available and absent. Initial test failed 1/1 on the actual command list versus expected empty list; isolated behavioral revert and full unchanged npm/Bun gates follow. Latest CodeRabbit body has no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-10-22T19:25:50.684Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOSfkApc6vLTfT fixed: assertReleaseTagHistory now supplies [] outside Git or when git cannot execute; alternative tracker workflows remain only in prose. Self-review checked every MissingTagHistoryError construction, its consumers and milestone diagnostics: shallow/no-tags cases retain executable fetch/config recovery; the remaining milestone-name placeholder belongs to a human-readable remedy, not this executable command list. Clarified usage and release docs. Behavioral revert: restoring only the prior assertReleaseTagHistory implementation makes node --test --test-name-pattern \"non-git tag refusals\" test/milestones.test.ts fail 1/1 (exit 1), actual two milestone workflow commands versus expected empty array. Restored source rebuilt; focused milestone suite 11/11, adjacent shallow/full/no-tags controls plus new regression 4/4, pm-linked new regression 1/1; all zero failures/skips. npm ci/build/build:test/docstring (18 files/180 declarations) and whitespace checks passed. Full npm/Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds follow after push; no old fix or history record was rewritten."
